    "schirmer-vascular-template-reference": {
      "id": "schirmer-vascular-template-reference",
      "modality": "Processed T1, T2 and FLAIR study templates, categorical regions and source-cell boundaries",
      "coordinate_context": "single-study-template-in-author-declared-MNI-source-world-mm",
      "title": "Vascular territories and posterior regions in matched template MRI",
      "src": "/app/anatomy/schirmer-vascular/index.html",
      "manifest_url": "/app/anatomy/schirmer-vascular/manifest.json",
      "sha256": "b7d53774159fef0f46a89ca227e65d54a73a7706027cfd5e38fbabc913eadd0e",
      "manifest_sha256": "85277d7ec002de3f5641f1bc6145a911dd8497b85cce272f23256faa1425d091",
      "caption": "Explore ten named source regions and one uninterpreted single cell in paired template MRI, source-label schematics and exact cell-boundary models. The source combines 16 older adults, including 12 with cerebral amyloid angiopathy and four controls. Names were associated with original numeric labels using the published figure. Pons/medulla remains combined; cerebellar and cerebral territories do not delineate individual arterial branches or all fine reporting anatomy. This reference is separate from the clinical source case.",
      "attribution": "Markus D. Schirmer, Anne-Katrin Giese, Panagiotis Fotiadis, Mark R. Etherton, Lisa Cloonan, Anand Viswanathan, Steven M. Greenberg, Ona Wu and Natalia S. Rost. Vascular Territory template and atlases in MNI space, version 1.0.0. Zenodo DOI 10.5281/zenodo.3379848. https://zenodo.org/records/3379848\nPublication: Spatial Signature of White Matter Hyperintensities in Stroke Patients. Frontiers in Neurology 10:208 (2019), https://doi.org/10.3389/fneur.2019.00208 . Figure 1 is reproduced without image modification.\nDataset and publication: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ .\nPrimer derivations: lossless source-plane packs, exact source-cell boundary meshes, native-label schematics, component navigation and publication-figure-derived numeric/name associations. Original source values, components and label 19 are retained. No patient registration, normal-population status, fine-anatomy completeness or clinical approval is asserted. No endorsement by the source authors or publisher is implied.\n",
      "source_url": "https://zenodo.org/records/3379848",
      "publication_url": "https://doi.org/10.3389/fneur.2019.00208",
